    "note": "clubs file their batting orders two to three hours before first pitch, so a card written in the morning stands partly on projected lineups — the nine each club is likeliest to field, taken from its own recent orders. Once the games have been played the real orders are known, and this is how those projections turned out: how many projected slots held the man who actually batted there, out of how many could be compared. Same man, same place in the order, counted slot by slot. Nothing on this page is weighted by this figure, no threshold is applied to it, and a projected game is excluded from every figure above rather than graded."
